Wave 2.5 slice 2 added useMoveEntityV2 as the template; Waves 2.7 and 2.8 followed it verbatim for useInteractV2, useTakeActionV2, useEndTurnV2. Each v1alpha2 unary RPC gets its own hook in src/api/use<Verb>V2.ts:

  export function useMoveEntityV2(): UseMoveEntityV2Result {
    const [loading, setLoading] = useState(false)
    const [error, setError] = useState<Error | null>(null)
    const verb = useCallback(async (...) => {
      setLoading(true); setError(null)
      const request = create(<Schema>, {...})
      try { return await encounterClientV2.<verb>(request) }
      catch (err) { const wrapped = err instanceof Error ? err : new Error('<Verb> RPC failed'); setError(wrapped); throw wrapped }
      finally { setLoading(false) }
    }, [])
    return { verb, loading, error }
  }

Invariants honored across all four hooks:
  - loading=true while in-flight, false on resolve/reject
  - error set on failure, cleared on next successful call
  - returned promise rejects on RPC error so callers can surface it
  - request constructed via create(<Schema>, {...}) from @bufbuild/protobuf
  - hook accepts plain JS shapes ({x,y,z}, {module,type,id}) and constructs proto messages internally; passes proto-shaped oneofs (e.g. ActionTarget) through unchanged so the caller controls the case

The client (encounterClientV2 in src/api/client.ts) is constructed from the gen'd v1alpha2 transport, mirroring the v1 client. Remaining v1alpha2 verbs (CreateEncounter, GetEncounter, SubmitCheck) follow the same shape — one file per verb in src/api/.
